<h2>Note Structure — Metadata and Progressive Disclosure</h2>
<p>Open a wiki note and it is laid out as <strong>title → metadata → body</strong>. If the body starts on line 38, for instance, then the <strong>37 lines before it are all metadata</strong>.</p>

<h3>YAML front matter is the heart of it</h3>
<p>The point where Obsidian is most valuable as a markdown editor is exactly this <strong>YAML front matter</strong> metadata field. It works on the same principle as the <strong>progressive disclosure</strong> we learned about in Claude Code.</p>

